WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.060
Your satellite passes over the same place at the same local time, every time.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.250
Why does that matter?

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:19.580
In 1972, the first Landsat satellite began photographing the whole planet.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:25.000
The record is now more than fifty years long, the longest of its kind.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.250
A sun-synchronous orbit turns with the seasons, about one degree a day,

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.730
so the lighting stays the same and changes on the ground are real.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.470
Healthy leaves reflect near-infrared light strongly.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.050
That lets us measure forest health from space.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:55.200
Landsat 9 flies at 705 kilometres and returns to each place every 16 days.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:01.800
Now compare your design. Every pixel is part of a story about forests and farms.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.730
<v Franchesca>Life leaves fingerprints in colour. From orbit, the planet is a living map.

